    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d515-a1">

                <pb facs="0647" n="605" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg605"/>

                <head>Mr. Watson to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">War Department</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington City</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-05-12"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 12, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Referring to previous correspondence upon
                    the subject, I have the honor, by direction of the Secretary of War, to enclose
                    herewith a printed copy of General Orders, No. 119, dated the 9th instant,
                    dismissing from the service Captain John A. Haddock, 35th regiment New York
                    Volunteers, “for violation of the sovereignty of a friendly foreign state in
                    arresting Ebenezer Tyler, a deserter from the United States forces, and bringing
                    him away from within the boundaries of Canada.”</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>P.H. WATSON, <hi rendition="#italic">Assistant Secretary of
                        War.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
